>
>Why can you die of starvation when you have full hit points?  I was of the

Poison can do the same thing.  Initially starvation was the most frustrating
problem I had with this game.  My latest character came equipped with a ring
of polymorph & polymorph control.  He never goes hungry ;^).

>opinion that hp reflected body condition,and the reason you starve to death is
>because your body condition deteriorates.

I don't think the starvation effect is intended to mimic reality, just to keep
the game difficult at all levels of play.

>                                         Similarly, I don't see why you should
>EVER starve to death while wearing a ring of regeneration.

SPOILER (rings and food):

All rings seem to take their energy directly from your metabolism, causing
the rate at which you need new food to increase.  The ring of regeneration
seems to be the worst of all.  Anyway, you don't really need a ring of
regeneration, after a while you will get the ability to regenerate without
the ring (I'm not sure if this is natural after gaining a certain experience
level, or if I get it from a certain creature that I always eat whenever I
can, due to repeated hints by Mr. Hairston)

>                                                            You should stay in
>the "Hungry" mode, but never further than that.  You may argue that you run
>out of energy to move, but it takes lots of energy to regenerate, and that's
>what the ring gives you.

The energy you are talking about isn't free, it comes from your food.

>  Of course, if the ring is working on your starvation, it won't be able
>to heal battle wounds very well, now will it?  :-)

There have been times I wish there was a "fill my belly" spell ;^).  But
that is what food is for.  Find food and live!  ;^)

SPOILER (polymorphing strategy for early game):

If you can manage polymorph, most monsters can eat almost anything and
get nutrition from it.  My favorite when I am early in the game is a
purple worm.  For him, eating is a way of life!  And once you get
satiated you still have really high hit damage.  The only thing I
don't understand is why my engulfing attack of a floating eye didn't
give me the intrinsic.  If I ate it and digested it, tell me why it
didn't affect me the same way as if I killed it first and then ate
the corpse?

Even if I have a ring of polymorph control early on, I don't use it
until after I've done a few random polymorphs.  Since the ring won't
let me choose a monster I don't know about yet, I let it change me
into random things until I become something dangerous.  Then I stick
with that for a while.  Now that I know that monster I can choose it
at will.

I haven't got a recent patch, so this is probably fixed now, but in
the version I'm playing, spending time polymorphing will eventually
result in a character with 18/** strength.  This seems to happen
whenever I "feel like a new man/woman".

If you can't polymorph, at least keep the rings off your fingers until
you need them.  You starve faster with rings on.

